1
00:04:46,363 --> 00:04:52,363
An army of forgotten heroes, all officially dead. They live
for combat. Now they've met the wrong man.

2
00:09:32,727 --> 00:09:38,727
Extreme Prejudice is a action, thriller, crime film directed by Walter Hill.

3
00:14:19,090 --> 00:14:25,090
Lean, mean Texas Ranger Jack Benteen locks horns with a former
friend, Cash Bailey, now a ruthless drug kingpin.

4
00:19:05,454 --> 00:19:11,454
Though they're on opposite sides of the law, they share
a love interest in the sensual Sarita.

5
00:23:51,818 --> 00:23:57,818
When a crew of rogue soldiers descends upon the border town for an off-the-books mission, all roads lead to a
bloody, to-the-death showdown, as loyalties shift and the lines between good and evil are blurred.

6
00:28:38,181 --> 00:28:44,181
Jack Benteen, played by Nick Nolte.

7
00:33:24,545 --> 00:33:30,545
Cash Bailey, played by Powers Boothe.

8
00:38:10,909 --> 00:38:16,909
Major Paul Hackett, played by Michael Ironside.

9
00:42:57,272 --> 00:43:03,272
Sarita Cisneros, played by María Conchita Alonso.

10
00:47:43,636 --> 00:47:49,636
Sheriff Hank Pearson, played by Rip Torn.

11
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
Sgt. Larry McRose, played by Clancy Brown.

12
00:57:16,363 --> 00:57:22,363
Extreme Prejudice is a 1987 American neo-Western action thriller film directed by Walter Hill, from a
screenplay by Harry Kleiner and Deric Washburn, from a story by John Milius and Fred Rexer.

13
01:02:02,727 --> 01:02:08,727
It stars Nick Nolte and Powers Boothe, with a supporting cast including Michael
Ironside, María Conchita Alonso, Rip Torn, William Forsythe, and Clancy Brown.

14
01:06:49,090 --> 01:06:55,090
Set in South Texas near the U.S.-Mexico border, the film's plot centers on the conflict between two former friends-turned-rivals, one a Texas Ranger
(Nolte) and one a drug trafficker (Boothe), who both become embroiled in a political conspiracy involving a black ops military unit.

15
01:11:35,454 --> 01:11:41,454
The film was released by Tri-Star Pictures on April 24, 1987.

16
01:16:21,818 --> 01:16:27,818
It received a positive critical response, but was not a financial success.

17
01:21:08,181 --> 01:21:14,181
Extreme Prejudice is an homage, of sorts, to The Wild Bunch, a western
directed by Sam Peckinpah, with whom Hill worked on The Getaway.

18
01:25:54,545 --> 01:26:00,545
Both films end with a massive gunfight in a Mexican border town.

19
01:30:40,909 --> 01:30:46,909
The title originates from "terminate with extreme prejudice", a phrase
popularized by Apocalypse Now, also written by Milius.

20
01:35:27,272 --> 01:35:33,272
The film explores themes of robbery, texas, mexican
standoff, texas ranger, organized crime.

21
01:40:13,636 --> 01:40:19,636
The tone is dark and emotional and intense.
